## figures/fig_mechanism.pdf — full width (`\linewidth`), teaser

**Supports:** collapse is decided early, near the collapsed solution, by a
per-direction competition between a driving force and a decay effect (theory,
Sec. 3).

> **Drive versus decay near the collapsed solution (illustration of the theory).**
> Per-direction reduction of the linear JEPA gradient flow:
> $\dot w_j = w_j\,[\,p_j s_j - (p_j^2 c_j + \lambda)\,]$,
> $\dot p_j = w_j^2 (s_j - p_j c_j) - \lambda p_j$, where $w_j$ is the encoder's
> norm along eigendirection $j$, $p_j$ the predictor eigenvalue, $s_j$ the
> context–target covariance, $c_j$ the context variance and $\lambda$ the weight decay.
> **(a)** Drive $p\,s_j$ (solid) and decay $p^2 c_j+\lambda$ (dashed) for two
> directions; a direction can grow only where drive exceeds decay (shaded growth
> window). **(b)** Trajectories of all 20 directions in the $(p_j, w_j)$ plane from
> the same near-collapsed initialisation ($w_j=10^{-3}$, $p_j=0.5$); color is the
> signal $s_j$. Near collapse the predictor receives no signal and drifts
> down at rate $\lambda$; directions that grow before $p_j$ leaves their window reach the
> non-collapsed fixed point (solid), the rest decay to zero (dotted).
> **(c)** The same directions over time: survival is settled in the first
> $\sim\!10^2$ time units, and the direction with $s_j=0.11$ in (a) collapses even
> though it has a growth window, because $p_j$ drifts out of it first.
> Parameters: $s_j$ log-spaced in $[10^{-2},1]$, $c_j=s_j+0.05$, $\lambda=0.01$,
> Euler step $\eta=0.01$, $6\times10^4$ steps; 7 of 20 directions survive.
> Computed from the theory's equations; not a measurement.

## tables/tab_heuristics.tex — text width; uses booktabs only

**Supports:** C3–C5 — each common anti-collapse heuristic acts through the
drive/decay balance. Rows follow paper-repo `sections/theory.tex` @ 80bb79c
(Props. window, survival, stopgrad, masking; Cor. depth; §Predictor scale and
learning rate for the weight-decay-convention dependence of the $\alpha$ row); the
substance is unchanged at 4a37f65. Theory-only at paper-repo's request (9-page body);
the measured counterparts are in Sec. 5, App. C and `fig_phase`. The weight-decay row is the
direct L2 coefficient $\lambda$ of the linear theory, whose boundary is calibrated in Tier A; the
Tier B AdamW doses are not mapped onto it (plan rev. 7).

> **What the common heuristics change, according to the theory.** For each
> heuristic: the term of the per-direction rate $r_j = p_j s_j - (p_j^2 c_j+\lambda)$
> that it changes, and the predicted effect on the rank of the learned
> representation. $\rho_j = s_j/c_j$ is the predictability of direction $j$,
> $c^t_j$ the target variance, $\Phi_j$ the survival margin of
> Prop. (survival), $\alpha$ and $\lambda_P$ the predictor's relative learning rate
> and weight decay, $S_k$ and $\sigma^2$ the input power spectrum and variance.
> The stop-gradient and weight-decay rows restate results of Tian et al. (2021) in
> our notation. $\lambda$ is direct (coupled) L2 encoder decay as in the linear model; decoupled
> AdamW decay in the nonlinear runs is not mapped onto it. The measured counterparts are in Sec. 5.

