## figures/fig_realdata.pdf — full width (about 2.1 in tall) — PARTIAL, rebuilt as Tier C runs land

**Supports:** P6 (C6), the transfer of the early-window statistic to real images, with the
frozen-backbone probe as a sanity check. Tier C uses the reference AdamW decay only and tests no
decay boundary. Input: experiment-repo
`results/raw/vit_runs/c_*/{summary,trajectory}_seed<N>.csv`, `data_provenance.json` and
`results/derived/vit_transfer_diagnostics.csv` and `results/derived/vit_init_probe.csv` (via
`probe_accuracy_init` in each summary) @ ae59eab. **Current state: 7 of the 18 Tier C runs**
(`c_reference` seeds 0–2, `c_scale_low` and `c_mask_low` seeds 0–1); panel (b) also has all 47 Tier B
runs of fig_nonlinear. The generator asserts the data provenance (HF revision `0b27149…`,
50,000/10,000 rows) for every run.

What it shows so far, so that the text does not claim more: the early positive-slope count does
**not** track the late rank in either tier. Counting all aligned directions gives 144–191 in 38 of
the 54 runs (all 7 Tier C runs: 166–188). The other 16 give 1–108: all six predictor-scale-2 runs,
3–27; the three EMA $\tau=0.9$ runs, 1–2; depth 3 seed 1, 25; depth 1 seeds 1–2, 108; and mask .25
seed 2 at all three decay doses, 52–62. Late ranks over all 54 are 28–156; the three $\tau=0.9$ runs,
with count 1–2, reach late ranks 89–113. Counting only directions resolved at step 25 (eigenvalue
$\ge10^{-3}$ of the largest) gives 0–45. In Tier B the rank is lowest at a checkpoint between steps
250 and 1,000 in 41 of 47 runs and grows afterwards (fig_nonlinear). On CIFAR-10 it drops by step 25
in all 7 runs (minimum 7–11) and grows mostly after the window (panel a). The late rank is therefore
set after the window the statistic uses. This is the regime P6 says to report. Neither count is a
linear-theory prediction (experiment-repo `results/README.md`, "Nonlinear early-rate sensitivity").
Panel (c): in all 7 runs the trained probe is above the same-seed initialization probe
(initialization 41.1–42.0%, trained 44.0–46.2%). Paired gain, mean with 95% $t$-interval, printed by
the generator: reference +3.1 pp [0.7, 5.5] ($n=3$); predictor scale 0.5 +3.6 pp [$-11.9$, 19.0] and
mask .25 +2.3 pp [$-1.9$, 6.5] (both $n=2$, so the intervals include 0).

